{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":987792,"ns":0,"title":"Barlow's wheel","extract":"Barlow's wheel was an early demonstration of a homopolar motor, designed and built by English mathematician and physicist Peter Barlow in 1822. It consists of a star-shaped wheel free to turn, suspended over a trough of the liquid metal mercury, with the points dipping into the mercury, between the poles of a horseshoe magnet.","description":"Early demonstration of an electric motor","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}